NEAR Protocol is a layer 1 digital network that uses a unique sharding technology called Nightshade to achieve scalability. It was launched in 2020 as a decentralized cloud infrastructure for hosting decentralized applications. NEAR offers cross-chain interoperability through Rainbow Bridge and a second layer solution called Aurora.
NEAR is a digital ecosystem that allows developers and entrepreneurs to create applications and protect valuable assets such as money, identities, etc., while making them easy enough for consumers to access.

In doing so, NEAR is creating the only community-driven cloud strong enough to expand its reach and future-proof it. Using shards, developers can write smart contracts and deploy them using processes very similar to how applications are deployed in centralized clouds.

How does Near work?
The Near Platform: Consists of a cloud of community-driven nodes. Developers can deploy smart contracts on this cloud without permission, and users can use the applications they use without permission. Applications that range from games to digital currencies can store their wealth (data) securely on the platform.

NEAR is the native token of the NEAR Protocol Ecosystem. It is used to pay transaction and storage fees. NEAR token holders can also receive rewards for storing coins on sites that work directly with the NEAR token or use them to vote on governance proposals. Near Coin is a natural asset of the Near ecosystem. Its functionality is available for all accounts.

Please note that there is no function for exchanging digital currencies in the application, but you can use the WARTA - NEAR Wallet application if you want to receive or send a NEAR token as quickly and comfortably as possible, or store a NEAR token with the convenience and reliability of our time.
